<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Caonabo</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. <a href="/years/1496">1496</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Caonabo was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/taino">Taíno</a> cacique of Maguana in central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hispaniola">Hispaniola</a> and husband of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anacaona">Anacaona</a> of Jaragua. He is credited with destroying <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/la-navidad">La Navidad</a>, the fort left by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/christopher-columbus">Columbus</a> in 1493, and killing its garrison. Captured by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alonso-de-ojeda">Alonso de Ojeda</a> through a trick around 1495, he died at sea in 1496 while being sent to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a>.</p></div>
